-- Phase 3 of the NPC / bestiary work, seventh book: every species in Rifts World
-- Book 14: New West (printed 127-171) - its five player races, the Psi-Ponies
-- and its "Monsters Common to the New West" - rows for creatures (migration 074)
-- and their attacks in stat_attacks (owner_kind 'creature').
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
-- The Cactus People, Fennodi, Keeper of the Desert, Lyn-Srial, Mountain Giant and
-- Psi-Pony are already published classes; these playable rows are the NPC view
-- of them. The Lyn-Srial is one row: its Sky-Knight and Cloudweaver print the
-- same basic stats. Every other animal and monster is an NPC.
--
-- NOT HERE: the Silonar (printed p.160), which reprints the Conversion Book One
-- block already live as `silonar`; the book's named people, who are not species.
--
-- A RIFTS BOOK: an M.D.C. creature's pool is its Main Body M.D.C.; the "on
-- S.D.C. worlds" figures and the M.D.C. by location are in pools_note. A printed
-- minimum speed above the dice's lowest roll is a "min N" floor. An I.Q. printed
-- only as words ("low animal intelligence") is left unrolled, the words in
-- pools_note. The Gwylack's P.B. is misprinted on the page ("1D$") and is left
-- unrolled rather than guessed; the Giant Canyon Worm's Spd is printed "12+12"
-- and is kept as printed.
--
-- EXTRACTED by four book-extract-workers, each given the NAMES of its species,
-- every number read off a 200 dpi render rather than the OCR cache, which carries
-- the digit cipher. RECONCILED by book-reconcile against the renders, row by
-- row; its corrections are applied. Every row passes creatureFormulaGaps, the
-- grammar the endpoint rolls with. description and natural_abilities are short
-- paraphrases - no sentence is the book's.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-creatures-new-west.sql
--
-- BY CATEGORY:
--   plant (1): Cactus People
--   humanoid (2): Fennodi, Lyn-Srial
--   mutant (1): Keeper of the Desert
--   giant (1): Mountain Giant
--   animal (15): Desert Sleeper, Duckbilled Honker, Great Plains Buffalo, Leatherwing,
--     Mammoth Brontodon, Moss-Back Scuttler, Ostrosaurus, Panthera-Tereon, Psi-Ponies,
--     Rhino-Buffalo, Tiger Claw Raptor, Tree Spiders, Tri-Tops, Tyrannosaurus Rex,
--     Whisker Coyote
--   monster (7): Devil Unicorn, Giant Canyon Worms, Great Dream Snake, Grigleapers,
--     Gwylack, Phantasm, Worm Wraith
--   demon (1): Oborus-Slitherer

  'cactus-people', 'Cactus People', 'plant', 'rifts', 1, 'Any (usually good or selfish)', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+8","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"2D6+6","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"2D6+6","PB":"2D6+2","Spd":"2D6+2"}', 'PE', '4D6+6', NULL, '4D6', 'ME', 'HP: plus 1D6 per level of experience (base is the P.E. attribute number). SDC: plus bonuses from skills; young get half. ISP: base is the M.E. attribute number, plus 1D6 per level.', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":2}', 'Horror Factor prints as 9+1D4 (base 9 stored; +1D4 residual not captured in horror_factor). Plus 3 to save vs disease. The two attacks per melee round only apply to those without combat training. Hand to hand basic can be upgraded to expert for the cost of two R.C.C. Related Skills.', 'Communicate via telepathy and empathy; Basic Math +20%, Botany +15%, Lore (two of choice) +15%, Holistic Medicine +15% (Cactus People only), Identify Fruit and Plants +20%, Wilderness Survival +15%, Land Navigation +15%, two Physical skills of choice, Hand to Hand Basic, two W.P.s of choice; six R.C.C. Related Skills at level 1; two Secondary Skills at levels 1, 4, 8, 10, 12.', 'Keen ultraviolet vision, resists disease, heals 2D6 hit points or SDC per day of sunlight (1D4 if cloudy or dark), survives up to a week without food or water.', NULL, 'Empathy, see aura, see invisible, and a natural no-cost telepathy with extended range to their own kind', '5 feet (1.5 m)', '150 lbs (90 kg)', '60 years; young born about every 18 months', 'Desert; near pre-Rifts ruins, abandoned vehicles, caves, canyons; live in wagons or shacks', 'Fennodi; Lyn-Srial; Cyber-Knights', 'Other humanoids; Slavers', NULL, 'Small, plant-based D-bee vegetarians with mild natural psionics and nutritious, slow-spoiling blood that draws predatory slavers and sorcerers.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.127');
  'fennodi', 'Fennodi', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but predominantly good (80%) or aberrant (10%)', '{"IQ":"3D6+2","ME":"2D6+8","MA":"2D6+10","PS":"2D6+10","PP":"2D6+8","PE":"2D6+8","PB":"2D6+2","Spd":"2D6+8"}', 'PE', '4D6', NULL, '4D6+12', 'MEx2', 'HP: plus 2D4 per level of experience. SDC: plus bonuses from O.C.C.s and skills. ISP: males M.E. x2, females M.E. x3, both plus 2D6 per level of experience.', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":2,"initiative":1,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"pull":6,"disarm":4,"roll":2}', 'Bonuses apply only at specific levels: parry +1 at levels 1,3,6,9,12,15; dodge +1 at levels 1,2,4,6,8,10,12,14; disarm +4 and pull punch +6 are flat; roll with punch, fall or impact +2 is flat; plus 1 to save vs Horror Factor at levels 1,3,6,9,12,15. Pin or incapacitate on a natural roll of 17-20 (must announce intent). Attacks: 2 at first level, plus 1 at levels 2,4,6,8,10,12,14. Generally fights only to escape or restrain; rarely kills.', 'R.C.C. skills in addition to O.C.C.: Wilderness Survival +25%, Land Navigation +20%, Prowl +15%, W.P. Blunt/Staff. Most (50%) are 3rd-6th level Cowboys or Saddle Tramps (1D4+2 levels); can also be Vagabond, Rogue Scholar, Rogue Scientist, Body-Fixer, Operator, Preacher, or Saloon Bum.', 'Keen infrared vision, plus 2 vs disease and toxins, immune to carcinogens and cancer, silent gliding movement, innate psionics that differ by sex.', NULL, 'Males: empathy, telepathy, sixth sense, mind block, empathic transmission, three healing abilities, plus a Protective Energy Aura and Ghost Walk (partial phase-out of physical reality); psychic affinity with the Whisker Coyote. Females: the same, including the Aura and Ghost Walk, except bio-manipulation and three physical abilities replace empathic transmission and the three healing abilities.', '7 feet (2.1 m)', '150-200 lbs (67-90 kg)', 'Not stated', 'Prairies and deserts of the American West, tending livestock as nomads; found throughout the West but far less common in the Canadian Wilderness', 'Cowboys; Saddle Tramps; Indians; Cyber-Knights; Sky-Knights', 'None per se, though frequently victimized by bandits, Psi-Stalkers, and supernatural menaces', 'Most (50%) are 3rd-6th level Cowboys or Saddle Tramps (1D4+2 levels); may also be Vagabond, Rogue Scholar, Rogue Scientist, Body-Fixer, Operator, Preacher, or Saloon Bum', 'Tall, quiet, peaceful nomadic D-bee herders known as the Quiet Walkers, gifted with sex-specific healing psionics and a defensive phase-out ability.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.128-130');
  'keeper-of-the-desert', 'Keeper of the Desert', 'mutant', 'rifts', 1, 'Any', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"2D4","Spd":"3D6"}', 'PE', '1D6x10', NULL, '3D4x10', NULL, 'HP: base is the physical endurance (P.E.) attribute number, plus 2D6 per level of experience. SDC: plus skill and O.C.C. bonuses. PPE: plus 1D6 per level of experience. M.D.C. is not automatically applicable; a character''s M.D.C., extra magic, and/or psionics instead come from a roll on the Random Powers and Deformities table (01-100), e.g. Super Psionics grants M.E. x10 ISP plus 2D4 per level, Indestructible Beauty grants 1D6x10 MDC plus 2D6 per level instead of HP/SDC.', NULL, 10, NULL, 'Horror Factor prints as 10+1D4 (base 10 stored; +1D4 residual not captured in horror_factor). Bonuses: None beyond the character''s chosen hand-to-hand combat skill. Their radioactivity means they generally cannot coexist closely with most races and may accidentally cause sickness or death nearby.', 'All have: Wilderness Survival +40%, Land Navigation +20%, Astronomy +15%, Botany (desert plants only) +15%, Basic Math +20%, Speak American 96%, Hunting, Track Animals +20%, Skin and Prepare Animal Hides +15%, Preserve Food +15%, Holistic Medicine +20%, plus two W.P.s of choice and five additional skills from Domestic, Physical, Technical, W.P., and Wilderness categories. Do not ride animals or pilot vehicles.', 'Nightvision 600 ft, impervious to radiation, resists heat and fire (half damage), senses water, surface or underground, 52% +4% per level; +4 to save vs horror factor and +5 vs possession; mildly radioactive to others; a further random mutant power or deformity is rolled at levels 1, 6, and 12.', 'None innately; a Random Powers and Deformities roll may grant spellcasting (e.g. fire magic, metamorphosis spells, summoning spells, teleport spells) at normal or reduced P.P.E. cost.', 'None innately; a Random Powers and Deformities roll may grant Super Psionics (base ISP M.E. x10, plus 2D4 per level) or immunity to psionics instead', 'Not stated (described only as human in origin and general shape)', 'Not stated (described only as human in origin and general shape)', '40-50 years; those above 35 are considered elders', 'The Salt Lake Desert, but comfortable in any desert', NULL, 'Most other humanoids; Most humans and many D-bees of the New West, who kill them out of fear', NULL, 'Deformed, radiation-mutated human outcasts descended from Salt Lake City survivors, each shaped by a randomly rolled mutant power or deformity.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.130-133');
  'lyn-srial', 'Lyn-Srial', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but 80% principled or scrupulous, 10% aberrant, 10% other', '{"IQ":"3D6+4","ME":"3D6+10","MA":"3D6+10","PS":"3D6+6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+4","PB":"3D6+8","Spd":"3D6+4"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx10', '1D6x10', NULL, 'MDC: plus 1D6 per level of experience. Spd is on the ground; flying speed is 3D6+20. PPE: plus 15 per level of experience.', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":3}', 'The book calls the fear-reaction stat ''Awe Factor'' (9+1D4) rather than ''Horror Factor'' - possibly a naming convention difference; base 9 stored, +1D4 residual not captured. Average NPC R.C.C. Bonuses: +1 initiative, +1 parry, +2 dodge in flight, +2 pull punch, +3 roll with impact or fall, +4 vs horror factor. The average Lyn-Srial is not trained for combat and will shy from violence. Sky-Knight and Cloudweaver variants share the same base stats above but differ in magic, skills, bonuses and equipment (see below); this single row covers all three.', 'Average NPC: History of their People 90%, native language 98%, three Earth languages +30%, literate in two Earth languages +10%, Lore: Ley Lines and Magic +10%, Law +20%, Basic Math +30%, Holistic Medicine +10%, Identify Fruit and Plants +20%, Wilderness Survival +15%, Land Navigation +10%, Sing and Whistle +20%, Dance +20%, Art +20%, Whittle/Sculpt +15%; six R.C.C. Related Skills at level 1 (plus two more at 3,6,9,12); two Secondary Skills. Sky-Knight variant (attribute req. IQ and ME 18+): four attacks per melee, Hand to Hand Expert (upgradeable to Martial Arts), extra combat bonuses (+1D6 PS, +2D6 MDC, +1D4x10 PPE, plus initiative/parry/dodge/roll/pull/disarm/horror-factor bonuses), W.P. Blunt, Paired Weapons, Ancient weapon and Energy weapon of choice. Cloudweaver variant (attribute req. IQ, MA and ME 18+): not trained for combat, three attacks per melee, R.C.C. bonuses of +2D4x10 PPE plus initiative/parry/dodge/pull/horror-factor-and-possession bonuses; skills emphasize history, language, lore, law, and art at higher percentages than the average NPC.', 'Supernatural strength and endurance, glows when happy or angry, regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. an hour and a lost limb in four months (an eye or tongue in a year), hawk-like vision (miles), nightvision 1000 ft, four arms with a bat-like membrane pair enabling flight and gliding.', 'Average NPC and Sky-Knight and Cloudweaver all know cloud of ascension, cloud surfing, aerial navigation, and globe of daylight as a baseline. Average NPC adds one spell per 3 IQ points from Clouds of Defense, Travel, or Survival. Sky-Knight adds all Clouds of War and Clouds of Peace plus one spell per level from any category except Clouds of Creation. Cloudweaver knows all Clouds of Defense, Travel, and Creation plus two additional Cloud spells per level from any category except Clouds of War.', NULL, '7-8 feet (2.1-2.4 m)', '200-320 lbs (90-144 kg)', 'Approximately 150-200 years, some to 350; most elders are 160 and up', 'Anywhere in the Americas, most numerous in the Southwest; hidden city in the Grand Canyon, Arizona; favor canyons, buttes, mountains and clouds', NULL, NULL, 'Sky-Knight requires I.Q. and M.E. of at least 18; Cloudweaver requires I.Q., M.A. and M.E. of at least 18 (both layered on the average Golden One''s base stats)', 'Tall, golden-skinned, four-armed, bird-like humanoids from another dimension devoted to peace, art, and cloud magic; some serve as warriors, others as scholars.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.133-136');
  'mountain-giant', 'Mountain Giant', 'giant', 'rifts', 1, 'Any', '{"IQ":"2D6+2","ME":"2D6+4","MA":"2D6+4","PS":"4D6+20","PP":"2D6+8","PE":"2D6+10","PB":"3D4","Spd":"2D6+10"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx2', '2D6', 'ME', 'MDC: plus 2D6 per level of experience, starting at level one. ISP: plus 2D6 per level of experience. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":2,"strike":2}', 'Horror Factor prints as 10+1D4 (base 10 stored; +1D4 residual not captured in horror_factor). Pin/incapacitate on a natural roll of 17-20 (must announce intent), critical strike from behind or on a surprise attack, body flip, plus 3 to roll with punch, fall or impact, plus 5 to save vs horror factor. Attacks: 3 at level 1, plus 1 at levels 4,7,9,12,15. Savage and merciless in combat; may eat part of a defeated foe as a symbolic gesture.', 'Speak American and Gobbledy 70%, Wilderness Survival +15%, Land Navigation +15%, Track Animals +20%, Track Humanoids +10%, Skin and Prepare Animal (and Humanoid) Hides +10%, General Athletics, Wrestling, Climb +15%, Swim +15%, Prowl +5%, W.P. Blunt, two W.P. Ancient of choice; four R.C.C. Related Skills at level 1; one Secondary Skill at levels 1,4,8,10,12.', 'Keen infrared vision, plus 2 vs disease and toxins, impervious to carcinogens, gentle and protective toward children and baby animals of any species, bonds with dogs and Dog Boys.', NULL, 'See aura, see invisible, impervious to fire, impervious to cold, impervious to poison, nightvision', '10-12 feet (3-3.6 m)', '600-800 lbs (270-360 kg)', 'Not stated', 'Rocky Mountains and the mountains/bluffs of The Bend in Lone Star; occasionally found elsewhere', 'Brodkil; Simvan; Dog Boys and other powerful beings, provided they do not try to control or enslave the giants', 'Humans and most other life forms (do not trust or like them)', NULL, 'Hulking, supernaturally strong bestial humanoid predators of the Rockies, savage toward adults but instinctively protective of children and animals.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.136-138');
  'desert-sleeper', 'Desert Sleeper', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist', '{"ME":"1D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"20+1D6","PP":"15+1D6","PE":"18+1D6","PB":"2D6+3","Spd":"34+4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '100+2D6x10', '2D6', NULL, 'MDC by location: Plated Head 100, Small Arms (2) 15 each, Hind Legs (2) 50 each, Underbelly 80; Main Body/Spine-Back (or curled into a ball) 100+2D6x10 on Rifts Earth. On SDC worlds: 2D4x10 Hit Points and 2D6x10 SDC with an A.R. of 16 instead. Speed has a stated minimum of 38 (26 mph/41.6 km); most individuals run 44-55.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":2}', 'Plus 4 leaping dodge, plus 3 to roll with impact or fall, plus 6 to save vs disease and poison, plus 2 to save vs horror factor (all in addition to attribute bonuses). Running head butt/ram knocks human-sized opponents back 2D8 yards. Curls into an armored ball defensively rather than fighting. Never attacks humanoids first, even when attacked.', NULL, 'Excellent speed, running six hours without tiring, and jumping (20 ft long, 12 ft high), goes up to 8 weeks without food or water by living off fat/water stored in its tail, tracks the scent of decay 55%, armor-plated head and spine, curls into a defensive ball.', NULL, NULL, '10-11 feet (3-3.3 m) head to tail, about 6 feet (1.8 m) at the shoulders', '600-800 lbs (270-360 kg)', '50 years', 'Deserts and grasslands of all kinds, cannot survive in climates cooler than 40 degrees Fahrenheit; most common west of the Rocky Mountains (Nevada, Utah, Arizona, deserts of California, Northern Mexico, and southwestern Texas/Lone Star)', NULL, 'Large predators; Pack hunters, including Silonar; Humanoids', NULL, 'Twice-human-sized, fast desert theropod dinosaur with an armored head and spine that curls into a defensive ball rather than fight; never attacks people first.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.138-140');
  'devil-unicorn', 'Devil Unicorn', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Always miscreant or diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+4","ME":"18+1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"30+3D6","PP":"18+1D6","PE":"20+2D6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"14+4D6 min 22"}', NULL, NULL, '200+1D6x100', '6D6', NULL, 'MDC by location: Horn 100, Head 100, Front Legs (2) 140 each, Rear Legs (2) 190 each, Tail 220; Main Body 200+1D6x100 on Rifts Earth. On SDC worlds: 1D4x100 Hit Points and 1D4x100 SDC with an A.R. of 17 instead. Speed has a stated minimum of 22 (15 mph/24 km). P.S. and P.E. are supernatural.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":3,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"pull":6,"roll":4}', 'Plus 3 to save vs psionic attack and possession, plus 12 to save vs horror factor (fearless), all in addition to attribute bonuses. Pounce attack carries a 01-74% chance of pinning prey helpless; after a successful pin, claws with all four legs for a massive 2D4x10 MD. Captures and holds up to 1D6 victims for prolonged mental and physical torture. Low human intelligence but a cunning predator; low, guttural speech in broken American.', 'Can learn to speak three languages at base skill level plus 6D6%, and knows a total of 1D4+2 skills limited to Rogue, Technical, and Wilderness categories. Does not advance in experience level.', 'Fair speed and stamina (runs 2 hours without pause), leaps 30 ft long or 20 ft high, strong swimmer (90% swim equivalent, holds breath 6+1D6 minutes, dives to 400 ft), climbs 90%/80%, prowl 60%, tracks humanoids 78% (60% for animals), land navigation 80%, wilderness survival 95%.', NULL, NULL, '5 ft (1.5 m) at the shoulders, 12-14 ft (3.6-4.3 m) body length plus a 10-12 ft (3-3.6 m) tail', '1.4 to 2 tons', '150 years', 'Any environment but favors mountains near people it can torment; most commonly reported in the Canadian Southwest, American Northwest, Wyoming, Colorado, Wisconsin, Michigan, and the Magic Zone', 'Others of its kind; occasionally powerful practitioners of magic or other powerful beings sharing agendas of mass murder, torture and mayhem', 'Large predators; Humanoids', NULL, 'Solitary, sadistic, single-horned quadruped supernatural predator that abducts and tortures captives for pleasure and terrorizes whole communities.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.140-141');
  'duckbilled-honker', 'Duckbilled Honker', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist', '{"ME":"1D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"20+1D6","PP":"14+1D6","PE":"18+1D6","PB":"2D6+3","Spd":"34+3D6 min 38"}', NULL, NULL, '100+1D4x100', '4D6', NULL, 'MDC by location: Head 100, Small Arms (2) 20 each, Hind Legs (2) 130 each, Underbelly 120; Main Body 100+1D4x100. On SDC worlds: 6D6x10 Hit Points and 4D6x10 SDC with an A.R. of 13 instead. Speed has a stated minimum of 38 (26 mph/41.6 km); most run 40-44 (about 30 mph/48 km).', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1,"dodge":2}', 'Plus 4 leaping dodge, plus 3 to roll with impact or fall, plus 6 to save vs disease and poison, plus 2 to save vs horror factor (all in addition to attribute bonuses). Rarely fights unless panicked, cornered, or defending nest/young; generally ignores small unmounted humanoids and flees danger. Travels in herds of 20-80, sometimes 100-600; herded like cattle by some Indians and ranchers.', NULL, 'Excellent speed, running four hours without tiring, leaps up to 8 ft, strong swimmer (equal to swim skill at 70%), holds breath underwater 1D4+3 minutes, goes without food or water up to six weeks, grinds plant matter with flat bill teeth, loud honking call.', NULL, NULL, '20-30 feet (6-9 m) head to tail, about 18-20 feet (5.4-6 m) standing erect', '2-3.2 tons', '30 years', 'Mixed conifer/oak forests; over a million believed scattered between the Rocky Mountains and the Mississippi River in the Central states, including Texas/Lone Star, with fewer in the east; in the west, greatest numbers in Oregon, eastern Wyoming, Nebraska, Missouri, Kansas, Oklahoma and Arkansas', NULL, 'Large predators; Pack hunters, including Silonar and Raptors; Humanoids', NULL, 'Massive herding herbivorous dinosaur-like grazer with a flat, duck-like bill, hunted for meat, oil, and hide, and sometimes ranched like cattle.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.141-143');
  'giant-canyon-worms', 'Giant Canyon Worms', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist or miscreant', '{"ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"24+1D6","PP":"12+1D6","PE":"20+1D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"12+12"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10+30', '1D6', NULL, 'On S.D.C. worlds the main body is 2D6x10 H.P. and 1D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 16. Digging speed is half normal Spd. Spd is printed "12+12", a fixed 24', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":3,"strike":2,"parry":1,"dodge":1}', '+3 to save vs psionic attack, +6 to save vs disease, +6 to save vs horror factor, impervious to poison.', NULL, 'Eyeless; tracks by smell 90%, by sound 70% and by vibration 70% (up to 4 miles); digs and burrows; dormant/starves up to 8 months; heat/fire half damage; cold double damage.', NULL, NULL, '25 to 40 feet (7.6 to 12.2 m) long', '4-12 tons', 'Estimated 20 years', 'Hot, dry deserts and arid land, primarily Arizona, Utah, and Mexico', NULL, 'Huge predators and humanoids', NULL, 'A blind, tunneling alien carrion-eater that smells blood for miles, then thrashes and pounds prey against the ground to kill it.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.143-144');
  'great-dream-snake', 'Great Dream Snake', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Generally anarchist or miscreant', '{"IQ":"3D6+10","ME":"3D6+10","MA":"3D6+10","PS":"3D6+12","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+10","PB":"2D6+8","Spd":"3D6+18"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx1000', '1D6x1000', '1D6x100', 'Adult (2000+ years) M.D.C. base is PE x1000 plus 2D6x10 per level of experience; Young Snake is PE x100 M.D.C. plus 1D4x10 per level. On S.D.C. worlds: Young has PEx100 H.P. and 1D4x10 S.D.C. per level with A.R. 15; Adult has PEx1000 H.P. and 2D4x10 S.D.C. per level with A.R. 17. P.P.E. Adult is 1D6x1000 plus 1D6x10 per level; Young is 1D6x100 plus 4D6 per level. I.S.P. is 1D6x100 plus 20 per level of experience. Horror/Awe Factor: Young 14, Adult 17 (formula and factor above use Adult). On the Astral Plane its M.D.C. is halved and it takes double damage there.', NULL, 17, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":5,"strike":3,"dodge":3,"pull":3}', 'Four attacks per melee, +2 for adults. +5 to save vs illusionary magic, +2 to save vs all other magic, +8 to save vs possession and mind control, +10 to save vs Horror Factor, impervious to poison and disease. At maximum size (100 ft) inflicts triple normal damage and M.D.C. increases 20 percent.', 'Basic math 98%, speak/read American and Dragonese 98%, land navigation 90%; learns 1D4 skills per level of experience with no category limits and a +10% bonus.', 'Nightvision 2000 ft; all dragon-like powers; shadow meld at will; unlimited shapeshifting (as Chiang-Ku); grows to 100 ft; poisonous bite; uses illusion and mind control to fake wish-granting.', 'Knows all illusionary spells plus spells level 1-5, call lightning, fire ball, wind rush, commune with spirits, memory bank, transferal, negate magic, dispel magic barrier, spoil, sickness, constrain being, banishment, summon shadow beast, time slip, mystic portal, anti-magic cloud, time hole, close rift, dimensional portal, teleport superior.', 'Knows all psionics at 10th level proficiency.', 'Varies from 3-100 feet (0.9 to 30.5 m) long', 'Varies with size; 10 lbs (4.5 kg) to one ton', 'Unknown; at least 100,000 years, may be immortal', 'Only known to exist in the American New West and Canadian Southwest', 'None known; rarely associates with own kind, dragons, or other supernatural beings', 'Unknown', NULL, 'A shapeshifting, possibly-dragon or demon rattlesnake god that manipulates dreams and false wishes, and devours those who challenge it.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.144-145');
  'great-plains-buffalo', 'Great Plains Buffalo', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animals; generally considered selfish alignment', '{"IQ":"1D4","ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"20+1D6","PP":"10+1D6","PE":"14+1D6","PB":"2D6+2","Spd":"20+2D4"}', '6D6+30', '2D4x10', NULL, '4D6', NULL, 'Spd has a minimum of 22 (15 mph/24 km). Horror Factor is none normally; 10 only when charging an opponent.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1,"dodge":1}', '+2 to save vs horror factor.', NULL, 'Fair speed; runs three hours without exhaustion; poor vision; keen sense of smell.', NULL, NULL, '8-9 feet (2.4 to 2.7 m) long, about 5 feet (1.5 m) at the shoulders', '800-1200 pounds (360 to 540 kg)', '25 years', 'Plains and prairies of the West; typical herds number 4D6x100', NULL, 'Large predators; pack hunters (including Silonar and wolves); humanoids', NULL, 'A once-endangered herd animal magically sent to another world and returned through a Rift, now roaming the New West in the millions.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.145-146');
  'grigleapers', 'Grigleapers', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered miscreant or diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+4","ME":"20+1D4","MA":"1D6","PS":"20+2D4","PP":"20+1D4","PE":"20+2D4","PB":"1D4","Spd":"30+3D4"}', NULL, NULL, '20+PEx2', '6D6', NULL, 'Minimum Spd is 33 (22.5 mph/36 km). Supernatural P.S. and P.E. On S.D.C. worlds: 2D4x10 H.P. and 5D6 S.D.C., A.R. 15. Horror Factor rises to 18 for a pack of 10 or more.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":4,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":4}', '+6 leaping dodge, +4 to roll with punch, impact or fall, impervious to poison, +12 to save vs horror factor (fearless).', 'R.C.C. Skills: Not applicable.', 'Strong runner and leaper (30 ft high/60 ft long); reluctant but able swimmer; excellent climber; prowls, tracks by scent and sight, navigates and survives in the wild at high skill.', NULL, NULL, '5 feet (1.5 m) long body plus a 7-9 foot (2.1 to 2.7 m) tail', '200 pounds (90 kg)', '25-30 years; litters of 1D4+1', 'Rocky Mountains and ruins of skyscrapers throughout the West, especially Colorado, Idaho, Wyoming, Montana, Oregon, Alberta, and the canyons of Arizona and Utah', NULL, 'Large predators; humanoids', NULL, 'An insectoid, four-armed pack predator bold enough to challenge Devil Unicorns, dinosaurs, or even a T-Rex or dragon.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.146-147');
  'gwylack', 'Gwylack', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, generally considered anarchist', '{"IQ":"1D4+4","ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"4D6+20","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"2D6+10","Spd":"1D6x10+20"}', NULL, NULL, '3D4x10', '1D4', NULL, 'On S.D.C. worlds: 2D4x10 Hit Points and 1D4x10 S.D.C., A.R. 12. P.B. is misprinted in the book ("1D$") and is left unrolled.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1,"dodge":2}', '+2 to strike with tail, +3 leap auto-dodge, +4 to roll with impact or fall, +8 to save vs horror factor, impervious to poison.', NULL, 'Nightvision 2500 ft; leaps 20 ft high/60 ft long; 320-degree compound vision, cannot be surprised; spins rope-thick webs; climbs sheer walls/ceilings; cannot swim and struggles badly if flipped onto its back.', NULL, NULL, '5 feet (1.5 m) tall, 8 feet (2.4 m) long, plus a 5-7 foot (1.5 to 2.1 m) tail', '300-400 pounds (135 to 180 kg)', '6-8 years; lays 1D4x10 eggs once a year', 'Dry desert regions of the New West: Lone Star, New Mexico, Arizona, Utah, Nevada, and Mexico', NULL, 'Humanoids; Leatherwings; various large predators', NULL, 'A venomous tarantula-scorpion hybrid hunted for food by locals despite one of the deadliest poisons in the Americas.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.147-148');
  'leatherwing', 'Leatherwing', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, generally considered anarchist or evil', '{"ME":"2D6","MA":"3D4","PS":"28+2D6","PP":"20+1D6","PE":"18+1D6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100', '3D6', NULL, 'Ground/climbing Spd is 3D6+6; flying Spd is 50+3D6 with a minimum of 55 (37.5 mph/60 km). Supernatural P.S. and P.E. Locational M.D.C.: Head/Beak 100, Wing Arms (2) 120 each, Hind Legs (2) 130 each, Wing Membrane (2) 130 each. On S.D.C. worlds the main body is 5D6x10 H.P. and 4D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 12.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":2,"roll":1}', '+6 to save vs disease and poison, +4 to save vs horror factor.; initiative: +2 ground / +5 flying with successful prowl; strike: +1 ground / +3 flying; dodge: +2 flying', NULL, 'Strong flier, five hours without rest; silent prowling dive attack; tracks by smell; hawk-like vision spotting prey two miles away; superb hearing.', NULL, NULL, '17-20 feet (5 to 6 m) tall, 15 foot (4.6 m) reach, 60 foot (18.3 m) wingspan', '1000 pounds (450 kg)', '30-50 years', 'Mountain and canyon cliffs, buttes and summits, especially Arizona, Utah, Nevada, New Mexico, and the Rocky Mountains; flocks up to 50,000', NULL, 'Humans; D-bees; Grigleapers; Panthera-Tereon; pack dinosaurs', NULL, 'A massive, sky-camouflaged flying reptile that snatches prey from cliffs or open ground, sometimes ridden as a Simvan raiding mount.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.148-149');
  'mammoth-brontodon', 'Mammoth Brontodon', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal scavenger, generally considered anarchist', '{"ME":"2D6+5","MA":"2D6+5","PS":"50+2D6","PP":"2D6+5","PE":"20+1D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"12+3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '350+1D6x100', '6D6', NULL, 'Supernatural P.S. and P.E. Locational M.D.C.: Horns (2) 100 each, Head 200, Mouth Claw-Fingers (2) 35 each, Forearms (2) 130 each, Hind Legs (2) 200 each, Tail 300. On S.D.C. worlds the main body is 1D4x100 H.P. and 6D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 14.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":4,"parry":2,"pull":3,"roll":1}', '+4 to save vs poison and disease, +5 to save vs horror factor.; initiative: +3 (olfactory); strike: +4 with tail / +2 with claws, horn, or bite; dodge: none', NULL, 'Slow but tireless (8 hours); superior sense of smell (identifies scents, tracks, and senses threats over a mile away, even underground or indoors); swims and climbs; strong land navigator.', NULL, NULL, '20 feet (6 m) tall on all fours, 50 feet (15.2 m) erect, 70-75 feet (21.3 to 22.9 m) long', '10-14 tons', '30-50 years', 'Light to dense forests, scrub, and prairie grasslands; seldom south of Colorado or Kansas; avoids deserts and canyons; herds of 4D6+10', NULL, 'T-Rex; small fast pack dinosaurs (Silonars, Ostrosaurus, Tiger-Claw Raptors); humanoids', NULL, 'The largest alien dinosaur-like omnivore on Rifts Earth, a favored Simvan mount and cargo hauler that flattens threats with tail and horns.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.149-151');
  'moss-back-scuttler', 'Moss-Back Scuttler', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, generally considered anarchist', '{"ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"22+2D6","PP":"2D6+4","PE":"20+1D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6+2"}', NULL, NULL, '250+1D4x100', '3D6', NULL, 'Supernatural P.S. and P.E. Locational M.D.C.: Head 50, Legs (6) 40 each, Tail 110, Underbelly (bottom shell) 100. On S.D.C. worlds the main body (top) is 6D6x10 H.P. and 4D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 18.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":2,"strike":4}', '+4 to save vs poison and disease, +6 to save vs horror factor.; initiative: +2 with tongue strike and tail attack; strike: +4 with tail / +2 with bite', NULL, 'Hard shell; slow; good vision and hearing; sticky prehensile tongue (4 ft reach); extendable head/neck; battering tail; competent swimmer and climber; prowls well.', NULL, NULL, '4 feet (1.2 m) tall, 12 feet (3.6 m) long, plus an 8 foot (2.4 m) tail', '1-2 tons', '150-300 years', 'Light to dense forested regions in the West, East, and Canada; rarely more than 2D4 in one region', NULL, 'T-Rex; small fast pack dinosaurs (Silonars, Ostrosaurus, Tiger-Claw Raptors); humanoids', NULL, 'A giant, moss-camouflaged land turtle that ambushes small prey with a sticky tongue and hibernates through cold winters.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.151-152');
  'oborus-slitherer', 'Oborus-Slitherer', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Always miscreant or diabolic', '{"IQ":"3D4+4","ME":"14+1D6","MA":"6+1D6","PS":"27+2D6","PP":"16+1D6","PE":"16+1D6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"20+2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '300', 'PEx10', 'MEx2', 'Minimum Spd is 22 (15 mph/24 km). Supernatural P.S. and P.E. Locational M.D.C.: Arms (2, huge) 120 each, Slug Portion of Body (center third) 200, Snake Portion of Body (last third) 180; Main Body (head and torso) 300 is on Rifts Earth. On S.D.C. worlds the entire creature has 260 Hit Points and 6D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 12. Considered a minor psionic.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":2,"disarm":3,"pull":4,"roll":5}', 'Six attacks per melee hand to hand, or two by magic. +5 to save vs possession, +9 to save vs horror factor.; initiative: +3 (+4 with tail attack); strike: +2 (+4 with tail); dodge: +2 automatic (no melee action used)', 'Prowl 60%, track humanoids 70%, track animals 50%, land navigation 80%, wilderness survival 95%; two ancient and one modern W.P.; learns three languages at base +30%; knows 1D4+4 skills from Communications, Military, Rogue, Technical, and Wilderness (all +20%); does not advance in experience level.', 'Excellent climber and swimmer; holds breath 12+1D6 minutes, dives to 1000 ft; resists heat and cold, half fire damage; regenerates 4D6 M.D.C. per minute; clings to walls and ceilings at half speed; long prehensile serpentine tail for whipping, entangling, or strangling.', 'Innate spellcasting equal to a 5th level sorcerer: chameleon, fear, turn dead, lesser paralysis, blind, agony, trance, calling, domination, fools gold, escape, tongues, fire ball.', 'Limited to presence sense and mind block.', '8-10 feet (2.4 to 3 m) main body and torso, plus about 30 feet (6 to 9 m) of slug and snake portions; 8 foot (2.4 m) reach', 'One ton', '200+ years', 'Anywhere in the Americas, most common in the Northwest, Magic Zone, and Canada; only 1000-2000 believed to exist, usually near populated areas', 'Other Oborus-Slitherers (groups of 3-6); other evil forces', 'Large predators; creatures of good alignment', NULL, 'A demonic hybrid of gorilla, snake, and slug that tortures and enslaves lesser beings, often allying with bandits, sorcerers, and demons.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.152-153');
  'ostrosaurus', 'Ostrosaurus', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered anarchist or miscreant', '{"ME":"2D6+8","MA":"2D6+8","PS":"22+2D4","PP":"14+1D6","PE":"18+1D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"88"}', NULL, NULL, '90+5D6', '3D6', NULL, 'I.Q. is given only as descriptive text (high animal intelligence and instincts), no die formula printed. Supernatural P.S. and P.E. M.D.C. by Location: Head 40, Front Legs (2) 30 each, Hind Legs (2) 50 each, Tail 40; figure above is Main Body. On S.D.C. worlds, Main Body is 2D4x10 H.P. and 1D4x10 S.D.C., A.R. 12.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":3,"roll":3}', '+8 leaping dodge; +4 save vs disease and poison; +6 save vs horror factor. Front claws used for dissecting prey and cutting meat.', NULL, 'Terrible swimmer but excellent climber; tracks by scent; spots prey a mile off; runs 60 mph without tiring for six hours; leaps 15 ft high and 40 ft long, farther with a running start.', NULL, NULL, '12-15 ft (3.6-4.6 m) long plus a 6 ft (1.8 m) tail; stands about 15 ft (4.6 m) tall', '1600 lbs (720 kg) average', '40 years', 'Light forests, hills and open grasslands, also hot arid steppes/savannahs of New Mexico and Central America; common along the Rockies and Montana, Wyoming, Colorado, Nebraska, the Dakotas into southern Alberta; prefers 50-100 F.', 'Commonly domesticated by Simvan', 'Large predators; pack hunters (including Silonar); humanoids', NULL, 'A fast, pack-hunting dinosaur predator favored by Simvan warriors as a mount; preys on herd animals, livestock and stray travelers on foot or horseback.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.153-155');
  'panthera-tereon', 'Panthera-Tereon', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist or aberrant', '{"IQ":"1D4+5","ME":"20+1D4","MA":"1D6+8","PS":"24+2D4","PP":"20+1D4","PE":"20+1D4","PB":"2D6+10","Spd":"20+3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '58+PEx2', '1D6x10', NULL, 'Supernatural P.S. and P.E.; minimum speed of 23 (15 mph/24 km). On S.D.C. worlds, Main Body is 2D4x10 H.P. and 1D4x10 S.D.C., A.R. 11.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":4,"strike":3,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"roll":3}', '+3 leaping dodge; +5 save vs poison; +9 save vs horror factor.', 'Not applicable.', 'Fast runner with brief double-speed sprints; leaps 50 ft high and 60 ft long; strong swimmer despite disliking water; excellent climber and tracker; detects ambush; skilled at wilderness survival.', NULL, NULL, '15 ft (4.6 m) long plus a 7 ft (2.1 m) tail', '1200 lbs (540 kg)', '30-40 years; litters of 1D4+1', 'Rocky Mountains and ruins of skyscrapers and tall buildings across the West, especially Colorado, Idaho, Wyoming, Montana, Oregon, Washington and Alberta, plus the canyons and mountains of Arizona and Utah.', 'None; predatory monster', 'Large predators; humanoids; loathes Grigleapers', NULL, 'An enormous sabertoothed cat with a black mane, a Rift arrival that stalks big game through mountains and ruins and, alone among predators, kills Grigleapers for sport.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.155-156');
  'psi-ponies', 'Psi-Ponies', 'animal', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but tend to be anarchist, unprincipled and scrupulous', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+12","MA":"3D6+4","PS":"6D6","PP":"3D6+4","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D6+12","Spd":"3D6+60"}', '5D6+6', '5D6+12', NULL, '6D6', 'ME+1D4x10', 'Typically Spd 66 (45 mph/72 km). +2D6 I.S.P. per level of experience; average level of experience is 1D4+3 for adults (4+ years old). Females also have healing touch, psychic purification, telekinetic force field, plus two of choice from healing or sensitive categories. Males have Psi-sword (a unicorn-like energy blade on the head) plus two powers of choice from the physical category. The book offers the Psi-Pony as an optional player character for players who can stay in character.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"dodge":3,"roll":3}', '+5 save vs mind control and illusionary magic; +5 save vs possession. Three physical or three psionic attacks per melee.', 'Land navigation (+20%), wilderness survival (+20%), astronomy (+15%), identify plants and fruit (+15%), herd cattle (+20%), track animals (+10%), basic math (+10%), plus understands 1D4 languages of choice (+20%). A willing rider gets +5% on riding skills (-15% if the creature does not want to be ridden).', 'Swims and jumps well; carries and pulls heavy loads; keen hearing; sensitive to the supernatural; lacks hands, though some overcome this with telekinesis or ectoplasm; major psionic, with powers varying by sex.', NULL, 'Major psionic. All start with empathy, bio-regeneration (self), mind block, sixth sense, and telepathy (own race only); see pools_note for sex-specific extra powers.', '14-16 hands (4.6-5.4 ft/1.4-1.48 m) at the shoulders', '800-1000 lbs (360-450 kg)', '16-24 years (10-15 for an ordinary horse)', 'Scattered throughout the New West and Southwest Canada; there may be as many as half a million.', 'Often work with Cyber-Knights; compassionate lawmen and other good (or aberrant) characters who do not try to enslave or imprison them', 'The Coalition (attacks on sight); humanoids who try to capture or enslave them; large predators including Panthera-Tereon, Leatherwings, lions and pack dinosaurs', NULL, 'An intelligent, golden-coated psionic horse-like animal that prizes its freedom; the book offers it as an unusual optional player character.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.156-157');
  'phantasm', 'Phantasm', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Generally anarchist or miscreant', '{"IQ":"2D6+8","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6+4","PS":"1D6+4","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"2D6+8","PB":"1D4","Spd":"1D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+PE', 'PEx10', 'MEx3', 'Spd is 1D6 walking, 11 flying (7.5 mph/12 km). A supernatural creature. +1D6 M.D.C. per level of experience (P.E.+6 H.P. and 5D6 S.D.C. with an A.R. 10 on S.D.C. worlds). +3D6 P.P.E. per level of experience. +2D6 I.S.P. per level of experience. Average level of experience: 1D4+4; uses the same experience table as the dragon.', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1}', '+3 save vs illusionary magic, +1 save vs all other magic, +8 save vs possession and mind control, +7 save vs Horror Factor, impervious to poison and disease. Three hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee, or two by magic. Vulnerable: rune weapons and weapons made from the Millennium Tree do double damage.', 'Basic math 98%, speak and read American and Dragonese 98%, brewing +10%, cooking +10%, palming +10%, pick pockets +15%, pick locks +10%, streetwise +10%, cardsharp +15%, ventriloquism +20%. Has little use for human skills.', 'Nightvision to 2000 ft; sees the invisible; keen vision and hearing; flies at will up to 200 ft altitude; bio-regenerates 3D6 M.D. per melee round; can induce temporary magical insanity (paranoia, obsession, phobia, panic attack or schizophrenia) on those who upset it.', 'Innate spellcasting: blinding flash, globe of daylight, cloud of smoke, ignite fire, armor of Ithan, befuddle, wisps of confusion, carpet of adhesion, blind, mute, agony, trance, calling, compulsion, luck curse, minor curse, curse: phobia, remove curse, memory bank, tongues, time slip, teleport: lesser, mystic portal, and dimensional portal.', 'Master psionic: bio-manipulation, mind bolt, mind wipe, mentally possess others, mind block auto-defense, group mind block, hypnotic suggestion, levitation, ectoplasm, telekinesis (lesser), and astral projection.', '4 ft (1.2 m)', '30-50 lbs (13.6-22.6 kg)', 'Unknown; lives thousands of years', 'Can appear almost anywhere, but seems to like the New West.', 'May ally with (or con) anyone it takes a liking to, or to trick/use a character for what it wants; tends to avoid practitioners of magic', '(none named - the book asks rhetorically: Does the average Phantasm really have any friends?)', NULL, 'A small, insane chimera stitched from a dozen animals that hoards magic items and gems, and lashes out with magic or psionics when startled.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.157-158');
  'rhino-buffalo', 'Rhino-Buffalo', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal predator, considered anarchist or miscreant', '{"ME":"2D6","MA":"2D4","PS":"28+1D6","PP":"16+1D6","PE":"26+1D4","PB":"1D4+1","Spd":"100+6D6"}', NULL, NULL, '150', '1D4x10', NULL, 'I.Q. is given only as descriptive text (animal intelligence, medium to low, but cunning and very ferocious), no die formula printed. Supernatural P.S. and P.E.; typical speed around 110 (75 mph/120 km). M.D.C. by Location: Head 60, Horn (1) 30, Front Legs (2) 90 each, Hind Legs (2) 80 each; figure above is Main Body. On S.D.C. worlds, Main Body is 2D4x10 H.P. and 2D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 14.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"roll":3}', '+6 save vs poison and disease; +9 save vs horror factor. Becomes frenzied in combat and frequently fights to the death (01-70%). Simvan warriors sometimes use it as a ferocious riding animal or giant watchdog.', NULL, 'Poor swimmer but excellent climber; tracks by blood scent and recognizes human blood; strictly carnivorous, preferring human prey; legs built for leaping onto prey, about 30 ft high and 60 ft long, farther with a running start.', NULL, NULL, '25 ft (7.6 m) tall and 40 ft (12 m) long', '5 tons', '30-40 years', 'Mountains, hills and rocky terrain with light forests and open grasslands; also hot arid plains of New Mexico, Arizona, Lone Star and Central America; common along the Rockies, Montana, Wyoming, Colorado, Nebraska, Dakotas, into Alberta and Saskatchewan; occasionally as far east as Ontario, Pennsylvania, the Virginias, Carolinas, Georgia and upper Florida.', 'None; animal predator', 'Favorite prey: Leatherwings, Duckbilled Honkers, Giant Canyon Worms, Mammoth Brontodons, Tri-Tops, buffalo and other large herd animals', NULL, 'A solitary, meat-eating predator resembling a rhino-buffalo hybrid, aggressive enough to attack armored giant robots it mistakes for rivals or prey.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.158-160');
  'tiger-claw-raptor', 'Tiger Claw Raptor', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered miscreant or diabolic', '{"ME":"10+1D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"19+1D6","PP":"19+1D6","PE":"19+1D6","PB":"2D6+4","Spd":"44+2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+34', '2D6', NULL, 'On S.D.C. worlds: 4D6+20 Hit Points, 3D6+12 S.D.C., A.R. 9. Females are 20% larger and have 20 more M.D.C. than males. Average speed 50 (35 mph/56 km). Horror Factor 12 for a pack of 4-8, 14 for 10+. I.Q.: high animal intelligence (no dice printed).', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":4,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":3}', '+6 to save vs horror factor, fearless in large packs.', NULL, 'Runs tirelessly for 8 hours; leaps 15 ft high and 20 ft long; survives two weeks without food or water; tracks scent 65%, prowls 86%, detects ambush 76%, climbs 75%/25%; spits blinding poison up to 20 feet.; vulnerable: cannot swim, and tends to underestimate humanoid foes', NULL, NULL, '5 to 6 feet (1.5-1.8 m) tall, plus a thin tail the same length as the body', '120 to 180 pounds (54 to 81 kg)', '35 years', 'Deserts and grasslands to forest and city ruins; most common in Arizona, New Mexico, Lone Star, Oklahoma, Colorado, Kansas, Nebraska and the southeastern territories', 'None, other members of their own species', 'Other predators and humanoids', NULL, 'A pack-hunting, striped theropod that studies prey for hours before ambushing with coordinated tactics and a blinding poison spit.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.162-163');
  'tree-spiders', 'Tree Spiders', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Alien predator generally considered Diabolic', '{"ME":"1D6","MA":"1D4","PS":"25+1D6","PP":"19+2D4","PE":"18+1D6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '200+3D4x10', '1D6x10', NULL, 'Supernatural P.S. and P.E. On S.D.C. worlds: 150 Hit Points, 4D4x10 S.D.C., A.R. 14. Mega-Damage by location: Eyes (10, called shot -3) 10 each; Tentacles (4 females/6 males, called shot) 42 each; Legs (6) 175 each. Attacks/Actions Per Melee: Females 5, Males 7. I.Q.: low animal intelligence (no dice printed).', NULL, 15, '{"initiative":1,"parry":3,"dodge":4}', '+5 on initiative from a silent tentacle attack (successful prowl), +3 to parry with tentacles, tentacles dodge at +4, +7 to save vs horror factor.', NULL, 'Prowls 70%, tracks by scent 70%; silent until striking, then slobbers; spots humans two miles away; resists heat and cold; immune to poison; regenerates 1D6x10 M.D.C. daily; regrows tentacles in 3D6 days and legs in a few months, but never its eyes; survives eight weeks without food.', NULL, NULL, '150 feet (46 m) from head to toe; tentacles reach 150 feet (46 m)', '1000 pounds (450 kg)', '30-50 years', 'Likely emerged from the Calgary Rift; found in forests of lower Canada and the old American Empire''s northern states, and in the West: Nebraska, the Dakotas, Colorado, Wyoming, Montana, Idaho, Washington, Oregon, Minnesota, Michigan and southern Canada', 'None', 'Grigleapers, T-Rex, and Leatherwings occasionally (and vice versa)', NULL, 'A tentacled, stilt-walking predator that ambushes animals and travelers from above, hauling victims up to a concealed mouth.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.163-164');
  'tri-tops', 'Tri-Tops', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist', '{"ME":"1D6+6","MA":"2D6+6","PS":"28+2D6","PP":"14+1D6","PE":"18+1D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"34+3D6 min 38"}', NULL, NULL, '200+1D4x100', '5D6', NULL, 'On S.D.C. worlds: 100+3D6x10 Hit Points, 4D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 13. Mega-Damage by location: Head 200; Horns (3) 60 each; Front Legs (2) 110 each; Hind Legs (2) 160 each; Underbelly 120. Minimum speed 38 (26 mph/41.6 km), most have speed 40-44 (about 30 mph/48 km). I.Q.: medium animal intelligence (no dice printed).', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":2,"roll":3}', '+2 to save vs disease and poison, +5 to save vs horror factor.', NULL, 'Runs without exhaustion for four hours; wades and swims at 55%; holds breath underwater 1D4+1 minutes; eats constantly yet can fast up to three months without ill effect.', NULL, NULL, '6 feet (1.8 m) tall at the shoulders, 25-30 feet (7.6-9 m) long', '4-5 tons', '50 years', 'Woodlands and scrub plains; over a million scattered between the Rocky Mountains and Mississippi River, particularly Washington, Oregon, Montana, Idaho, Wyoming, Colorado, the Dakotas, Minnesota, Nebraska, Kansas and parts of Canada', 'None', 'Large predators, pack hunters (including Silonar and Raptors), and humanoids', NULL, 'A three-horned, herd-forming herbivore with a bony neck shield, normally passive but capable of a devastating charging ram.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.164-166');
  'tyrannosaurus-rex', 'Tyrannosaurus Rex', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"ME":"1D6+6","MA":"2D6","PS":"50+2D6","PP":"14+1D6","PE":"23+1D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"34+3D6 min 38"}', NULL, NULL, '400+1D4x100', '5D6', NULL, 'On S.D.C. worlds: 200+4D6x10 Hit Points, 1D4x100 S.D.C., A.R. 12. Mega-Damage by location: Head 280; Forearms (2, useless) 40 each; Hind Legs (2) 300 each; Tail 220; Underbelly 300. Minimum speed 38 (26 mph/41.6 km), most have speed 40-44 (about 30 mph/48 km). I.Q.: medium to low animal intelligence (no dice printed).', NULL, 18, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"roll":2}', '+5 to save vs disease and poison, +10 to save vs horror factor.', NULL, 'Sprints at full speed only fifteen minutes, otherwise moves at half speed; can fast up to two months; exceptional smell and hearing smell blood or carrion up to 1.5 miles (2.4 km) away; tracks by smell 80%, recognizes scents 80%.; vulnerable: soft underbelly, useless forearms, hates water and cannot swim', NULL, NULL, '30 feet (9 m) tall and 50 feet (15.2 m) long', '5-6 tons', '25 years', 'Throughout the New West and southwestern Canada; most numerous in Montana, Idaho and Wyoming', 'None; solitary or hunts in small groups of 2-4', 'Large predators, pack hunters (including Silonar and Raptors), and humanoids', NULL, 'A massive apex predator and scavenger with a crushing bite, weak forearms, and an exposed underbelly, unable to swim.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.166-167');
  'whisker-coyote', 'Whisker Coyote', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered anarchist, unprincipled and scrupulous', '{"ME":"1D6+12","MA":"2D6+10","PS":"1D6+10","PP":"1D6+12","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"2D6+6","Spd":"2D6+34"}', '5D6+6', '4D6+6', NULL, '5D6', 'MEx2+1D4', 'I.S.P. total is M.E. x2 +1D4, gained per level of experience. Fennodi companion-sensing rapport range 3000 ft. Senses magic/ley lines/supernatural beings to 1000 ft, ley line storms or dimensional anomalies to 1 mile. Estimated population: 1-3 million in the New West, about 1 million in Mexico, under 100,000 east of the Mississippi. I.Q.: high animal intelligence, about a child''s (no dice printed).', 10, 9, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":2,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":3}', '+6 to save vs poison and disease, +1 to save vs psionic attack, +4 to save vs mind control and possession, +3 to save vs horror factor.', NULL, 'Runs four hours without tiring; leaps eight feet long, four feet high; survives three days without food or water; omnivorous scavenger; tracks by scent 80%, swims 60%, prowls 55%, climbs 65%; sees the invisible and psionics.', NULL, 'Major psionic: sense evil, sense magic (triple range), see aura, mind block, empathy; senses magic/ley lines/supernatural beings to 1000 ft and ley line storms or dimensional anomalies to 1 mile; immune to Simvan/Psi-Stalker psionic empathy and control.', '3 feet (0.9 m) at the shoulders, 4 feet (1.2 m) long', '40-55 pounds (18-24.7 kg)', '25 years', 'Prairies, grasslands and deserts, but flourishes almost anywhere except tropical or arctic climates; avoids Canada', 'Strange attraction and friendship to Fennodi; Humans and many types of D-bees', 'Large predators and humanoids; Disliked and feared by Simvan, Psi-Stalkers, the Minions of Splugorth and all supernatural beings', NULL, 'A small alien canine with prehensile facial tentacles and near-human intellect, fiercely loyal to companions and psionically drawn to Fennodi.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.167-168');
  'worm-wraith', 'Worm Wraith', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6","PS":"4D6+20","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"2D6+10","PB":"1D4","Spd":"2D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '4D4x10', '4D6x10', '2D6+40', 'Supernatural P.S. and P.E. M.D.C. is roughly 3 per worm, with 40-60 worms per Worm Wraith. P.P.E. is roughly 1D4 per worm. I.S.P. is 1 per worm (average worm count 2D6+40). Attacks per melee increase by +1 at levels 2, 4, 8, 12 and 15. Actual Horror Factor roll is 11+1D4.', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1}', '+8 to save vs horror factor; impervious to all forms of possession.', 'Prowl 80%, Land Navigate 90%, Wilderness Survival 90%, Intelligence 80%, Track Humanoids 60%, Detect Ambush 60%, Climb 70%/60%, Swim 70%, Basic Math 80%, Horsemanship General, Horsemanship Exotic, Paired Weapons and Quick Draw (same as the Gunfighter), W.P. Revolvers, W.P. Pistols, W.P. Two Modern of choice, plus two Secondary Skills at levels 1, 3, 6, 9 and 12 from Rogue, Technical, W.P. and Wilderness.', 'Senses via an unknown mechanism despite no visible organs; nightvision 1000 feet; tracks scent and decay 60-80%; impervious to disease, poison, heat and cold; fire does half damage; fully regrows from one surviving worm in 2D4 days; can send out 2 or 4 worms as spies (prowl 90%, climb 90%/70%) that report all they saw on rejoining the body.', 'Turn dead, repel animals, breathe without air, shadow meld', 'Minor psionic: Empathy, object read, sixth sense, mind block auto-defense; telepathic link (unlimited range) to the alien intelligence that created it, and to other Worm Wraiths within 500 ft (152 m)', '6 feet (1.8 m), average', '300 pounds (135 kg)', NULL, 'Northwest: scarce, hunts alone, in pairs, or small groups of 1D4+3, rare east of Colorado. Southwest: increasing, often bands of 12-36 on murderous rampages', 'Sometimes associate with necromancers, evil practitioners of magic, Brodkil and other lesser demons', 'All intelligent mortal beings, particularly humans and Psi-Stalkers, and anybody who gets in their way', NULL, 'A demonic gunslinger built from dozens of writhing worms in human shape, hunting humanoids with firearms, ambush tactics and near-total regeneration.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.168-171');




